  m_Name: 1966 vandalism
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: Severe Vandalism Laws 1966
  info: "The Vandalism Act imposes harsh penalties for defacing or damaging public
    and private property. This includes graffiti, unauthorized posters, and tampering
    with vehicles. Offenders can face fines of up to SGD 2,000, imprisonment of up
    to three years, and corporal punishment in the form of caning. The law aims to
    maintain Singapore\u2019s reputation for orderliness and discourage acts of defacement
    that detract from the city\u2019s clean and organized image."
  image: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 5115cf0708ef747f380fc999d1132c61, type: 3}
